        "note": "<div class=\"Example\"><table class=\"example\"><tr><td><p><i>nii</i></p></td><td><p>2nd sg. fam.</p></td><td><p>- familiar form of address, derives historically fromProto-Tamil <i>niin</i></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><i>niinkaL</i></p></td><td><p>2nd pl. fam.</p></td><td><p>- according to  ), <i>niinkaL</i></p><p>derives historically from the repluralization of the Proto-Tamil2nd pl form <i>niim</i> + <i>kaL</i> 'pl';</p><p>- this form is used as familiar form of plural address</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><i>niinkaL</i></p></td><td><p>2nd sg. hhon.</p></td><td><p>- more polite form of address than <i>niir</i>;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><i>niir</i></p></td><td><p>2nd sg. hon.</p></td><td><p>- polite form of address, derives historically from the old sg<i>niin</i> + <i>yir</i> 'pl'</p></td></tr></table></div>",
